00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.216
okay, you're a hooker, and it's just--

00:01:13.216 --> 00:01:14.357
(laughing)

00:01:14.357 --> 00:01:15.850
it didn't make any sense.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.270
- No I meant like when she does

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:18.660
a place where she doesn't belong.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.820
All right where are you at right now, Jay?

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.110
- We're just crossing
into another building,

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.503
I want to show you,

00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:27.990
I like cars that have
sometimes you buy the story

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.240
as much as you buy the car.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.220
Like the cars I'm
standing in front of now.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.530
These are both Hudson Hornets,

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.550
this is a 1953, it's a 1951.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.870
I bought this one first and I restored it,

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.575
and then one day I got a call
from a 94 year old woman,

00:01:42.575 --> 00:01:43.408
and she said,

00:01:43.408 --> 00:01:44.910
I understand you like cars,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.080
my husband and I bought a
brand-new '51 Hudson Hornet,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.040
in '51 and we drove it from
New Jersey with our family

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.490
to our new life in California,

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.114
and he died in '96.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.455
This is back in 2004.

00:01:57.455 --> 00:01:59.760
She said, would you be
interested in buying the car?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.210
And I said, well I already
have a Hudson Hornet.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:03.043
She goes,

00:02:03.043 --> 00:02:04.470
well, it's a wonderful car,

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.530
would you just come look at it?

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.363
All right.

00:02:07.363 --> 00:02:09.260
So I drive up there, 94 years old,

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:10.790
no hearing aid, no glasses,

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.123
looks like she's 60.

00:02:13.231 --> 00:02:14.064
So she shows me the car

00:02:14.064 --> 00:02:15.520
and it's got four flat tires,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.550
it'd been sitting for 20 years

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.500
but he died in like '96, this was 2004.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.420
She goes, well will you
give me $5,000 for it?

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.300
I said, well, all right, okay.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.870
So I bought it, I felt sorry.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.730
Then I brought it back to my garage.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.420
Took about two years to restore it.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.880
And I figure, why don't I
see if she's still alive.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.540
So I dialed the number and, "Hello?"

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.810
I go, hi, it's Jay Leno.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:35.710
Oh Mr. Leno!

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.420
Now she's 96 and I said, listen,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.290
I finished the car, it looks brand-new,

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.327
do you want to go for a ride?

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.840
"Oh I gotta get my hair
done, oh my god, I gotta--"

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:45.673
I said, yeah.

00:02:45.673 --> 00:02:47.900
And she goes, can the kids come?

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.810
I go, well sure.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.725
Well her kids are 74 and 72.

00:02:51.725 --> 00:02:53.870
(laughing)

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:54.770
So we're driving along,

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.280
she's telling me stories about

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.970
you know, coming across Route 66

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.010
back in the '50s and what it was like.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.400
Meanwhile the two kids in the back

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.510
start poking each other like this.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.180
So she turns back, she goes, I don't--

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.013
(slapping)

00:03:08.013 --> 00:03:10.667
She just starts slapping
the crap out of them!

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:12.219
Just whacking over the head.

00:03:12.219 --> 00:03:14.080
And the three of them are just laughing

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.397
and falling down, they're just hysterical.

00:03:16.397 --> 00:03:19.266
"I told you kids to behave,
Mr. Leno gave us a ride."

00:03:19.266 --> 00:03:21.423
And she's just whacking
them and whacking them.

00:03:21.423 --> 00:03:23.740
And the three of them
are laughing so hard.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.296
And it was really the time of my life,

00:03:26.296 --> 00:03:27.129
it was just a wonderful--

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:28.939
she lived to be 104 years old.

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:29.980
- Wow.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.090
- But she had such fun going for a ride

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.030
in the car,

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.320
with the two kids,

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.270
and you know that's
what makes this car kind

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.530
of special, it's not really a special car

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.950
until you know those stories.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.540
The only car they had,

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.070
and the 72 year old and
the 74 year old told me

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.220
when they were teenagers,

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.040
they were so embarrassed
that their parents' car

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.010
was 16 years old,

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.360
that they would have
their dad drop them off

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.850
like three blocks from the school

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.070
and then they would walk to school

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.770
so other kids wouldn't see

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.160
that their dad drove a 1951 car.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.500
Of course now it's a
classic, but back then,

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.965
that was a whole different story.

00:04:02.965 --> 00:04:04.047
So that's, you know,

00:04:04.047 --> 00:04:06.390
that's a car with a pretty good story.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.290
- Well can we see another
car you have in there?

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.901
- This is my '55 Buick Roadmaster.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.723
When I came to Los Angeles,

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.610
I got off the plane at LAX,

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.070
I immediately went to the newsstand,

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.700
I bought a copy of the pennysaver,

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.260
that's like one of those
advertising magazines, you know.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.010
You buy things for sale.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.850
And I was looking for a car, 'cause in LA

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.990
you need a car before
you need a place to live

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.720
because you can't get to the
place you live unless you

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:32.690
have a car.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:37.690
So I saw this advertised
at $350 and I bought it,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.570
and I've had it since 1972.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.150
I met my wife in this car,

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.660
we dated in this car,

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:44.960
got married in this car,

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.710
I took this car to my first Tonight Show

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.610
and I took it to my last Tonight Show.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:50.966
I'll tell you the story,

00:04:50.966 --> 00:04:54.270
my wife hates this story,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.660
but it's kind of funny

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.860
'cause we had our first encounter

00:04:58.860 --> 00:04:59.835
in this car,

00:04:59.835 --> 00:05:01.448
(laughing)

00:05:01.448 --> 00:05:03.050
- Encounter.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:03.883
- Encounter,

00:05:03.883 --> 00:05:05.270
and on our 25th wedding anniversary,

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.700
I said, let's try and recreate that.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.827
So we both got in the car

00:05:08.827 --> 00:05:12.240
